      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To completely factor the expression \\(9x^2 + 3x\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Factor out the greatest common factor (GCF):**\n   - Identify the GCF of the terms in the expression. The GCF of \\(9x^2\\) and \\(3x\\) is \\(3x\\).\n   - Factor \\(3x\\) out of each term in the expression:\n     \\[\n     9x^2 + 3x = 3x(3x) + 3x(1) = 3x(3x + 1)\n     \\]\n     Here, \\(3x\\) is factored out, and the remaining terms inside the parentheses are \\(3x\\) and \\(1\\).\n\n2. **Write the final factored form:**\n   - The expression \\(9x^2 + 3x\\) in its fully factored form is:\n     \\[\n     3x(3x + 1)\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the completely factored form of the expression \\(9x^2 + 3x\\) is \\boxed{3x(3x + 1)}.",
